emoji_picker_overhaul.s:
REWORK the shared EmojiPicker component (src/lib/components/EmojiPicker.svelte, 51 lines) so it stops being a wall of 1923 tiny emojis, and update its vitest. Used identically in both room and DM chat, so one change fixes both.

CURRENT BUGS (from live browser DOM probe + code read):
1. Card is w-[300px] fixed inside the 560px modal -> wastes the modal width, picker looks tiny.
2. grid-cols-8 text-[20px] max-h-[240px] -> 1923 flat buttons, ~48 screens of scrolling, no anchors while scrolling.
3. Category tabs are tiny 11px text, horizontally scrollable, and disappear entirely during search.
4. No recent/frequently-used row; every pick requires re-hunting the same emoji.

REPLACEMENT (write the whole file; Svelte 5 runes, no comments, design tokens only):
<script lang="ts">
	import { onMount } from 'svelte';
	import { EMOJIS, GROUPS, search_emoji } from '$lib/emoji';
	let { onselect, onclose }: { onselect: (emoji: string) => void; onclose: () => void } = $props();
	let q = $state('');
	let activeGroup = $state<number | null>(null);
	let recent = $state<string[]>([]);
	const RECENT_KEY = 'x2:recent_emojis';
	const RECENT_MAX = 12;

	onMount(() => {
		try {
			recent = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(RECENT_KEY) ?? '[]');
		} catch {}
	});

	function pick(e: string) {
		recent = [e, ...recent.filter((x) => x !== e)].slice(0, RECENT_MAX);
		try {
			localStorage.setItem(RECENT_KEY, JSON.stringify(recent));
		} catch {}
		onselect(e);
	}

	const label_of = (e: string): string => EMOJIS.find((x) => x.emoji === e)?.label ?? e;
	const searching = $derived(q.trim() !== '');
	const results = $derived(
		searching
			? search_emoji(q)
			: activeGroup === null
				? EMOJIS
				: EMOJIS.filter((e) => e.group === activeGroup)
	);
	const sections = $derived(
		searching || activeGroup !== null
			? []
			: GROUPS.map((g) => ({ ...g, emojis: EMOJIS.filter((e) => e.group === g.key) }))
	);
</script>

<div
	class="flex w-full flex-col rounded-[14px] border border-line bg-panel-solid p-3 shadow-lg"
	role="dialog"
>
	<input autofocus class="mb-2 text-[13px]" placeholder="search emoji…" bind:value={q} />
	{#if !searching && recent.length}
		<div class="mb-2">
			<div class="mb-1 text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-mute">recent</div>
			<div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-1">
				{#each recent as e (e)}
					<button
						type="button"
						class="rounded-[6px] p-1 text-[22px] hover:bg-panel"
						aria-label={'recent ' + label_of(e)}
						onclick={() => pick(e)}
						>{e}</button
					>
				{/each}
			</div>
		</div>
	{/if}
	{#if !searching}
		<div class="mb-2 flex gap-1 overflow-x-auto">
			<button
				type="button"
				class="btn px-2 py-1 text-[11px]"
				class:btn-amber={activeGroup === null}
				onclick={() => (activeGroup = null)}
				>all</button
			>
			{#each GROUPS as g (g.key)}
				<button
					type="button"
					class="btn shrink-0 px-2 py-1 text-[11px]"
					class:btn-amber={activeGroup === g.key}
					onclick={() => (activeGroup = g.key)}
					>{g.label}</button
				>
			{/each}
		</div>
	{/if}
	<div class="max-h-[min(60dvh,480px)] overflow-y-auto">
		{#if sections.length}
			{#each sections as s (s.key)}
				<div
					class="sticky top-0 z-10 border-b border-line bg-panel-solid px-1 py-1.5 text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-mute"
					>{s.label}</div
				>
				<div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-1 pb-2">
					{#each s.emojis as e (e.emoji)}
						<button
							type="button"
							class="rounded-[6px] p-1 text-[22px] hover:bg-panel"
							title={e.label}
							onclick={() => pick(e.emoji)}
							>{e.emoji}</button
						>
					{/each}
				</div>
			{/each}
		{:else}
			<div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-1">
				{#each results as e (e.emoji)}
					<button
						type="button"
						class="rounded-[6px] p-1 text-[22px] hover:bg-panel"
						title={e.label}
						onclick={() => pick(e.emoji)}
						>{e.emoji}</button
					>
				{/each}
			</div>
		{/if}
	</div>
</div>

WHY this shape: w-full fills the 560px modal (was 300px); grid-cols-12 + text-[22px] shows ~2.5x more per screen; sticky section headers (Slack-style) give in-wall anchors for the 'all' view; recent row (localStorage, capped 12, deduped, reordered-most-recent-first) removes the re-hunt; autofocus lets you type to filter immediately; tabs stay hidden during search (existing behavior). All emoji buttons route through pick() so every selection also updates recents.

TESTS (src/lib/components/__tests__/EmojiPicker.svelte.test.ts, 43 lines). Keep the existing 4 tests verbatim (they must still pass: title 'grinning face' still exists in the smileys section; 'all' tab present default; search hides tabs; category click narrows). Add to the describe block:
	beforeEach(() => localStorage.clear());
Add 2 new tests:
	it('renders sticky group section headers in the all view', () => {
		render(EmojiPicker, { props: { onselect: vi.fn(), onclose: vi.fn() } });
		const matches = screen.getAllByText('smileys & emotion');
		expect(matches.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(2);
	});
	it('persists picked emojis to localStorage and shows a recent row', async () => {
		const onselect = vi.fn();
		render(EmojiPicker, { props: { onselect, onclose: vi.fn() } });
		await fireEvent.click(screen.getByTitle('grinning face'));
		expect(onselect).toHaveBeenCalledWith('😀');
		expect(localStorage.getItem('x2:recent_emojis')).toContain('😀');
		expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /recent grinning face/ })).toBeInTheDocument();
	});
(The 'smileys & emotion' label appears both as a tab button and as a section header in the all view, so >=2 proves headers render. jsdom provides localStorage.)

NOTE: 'grinning face' has emoji '😀' (emojibase FE0F-stripped char is the same test already asserts).

PHASES: 1) write the 2 new tests + beforeEach, 2) run pnpm vitest run src/lib/components/__tests__/EmojiPicker.svelte.test.ts and watch the 2 new tests FAIL (no recent row / no section headers in the old component), 3) implement the component rewrite above, 4) rerun the same file: all 6 tests pass. Then run pnpm test (full) and pnpm check — both green before marking done.

room_composer_emoji.s:
ADD a composer emoji button to the ROOM chat page (src/routes/app/rooms/[id]/+page.svelte, 802 lines) that opens EmojiPicker in 'insert into message' mode — selecting an emoji splices it into the message text input at the cursor, not as a reaction. This is the discoverability fix: currently the ONLY way to open the emoji picker anywhere is the hidden hover 'react' button on a message bubble (line 646-675: opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100), while stickers have a permanent composer button (lines 764-772).

EDIT 1 — line 4: `import { onMount, onDestroy } from 'svelte';` becomes:
	import { onMount, onDestroy, tick } from 'svelte';

EDIT 2 — lucide import block (lines 20-30, currently `import { ArrowLeft, Image, Send as SendIcon, Phone, PhoneOff, Mic, MicOff, Video, VideoOff } from '@lucide/svelte';`): add `Smile,` to the list. (Verified: @lucide/svelte 1.27.0 ships icons/smile.svelte.)

EDIT 3 — right after `let stickerOpen = $state(false);` (line 175) insert:
	let emojiOpen = $state(false);
	let composerInput: HTMLInputElement | undefined = $state();
	let emojiCursor = $state(0);

	function openEmoji() {
		emojiCursor = composerInput?.selectionStart ?? text.length;
		emojiOpen = true;
	}

	function insertEmoji(e: string) {
		emojiOpen = false;
		text = text.slice(0, emojiCursor) + e + text.slice(emojiCursor);
		emojiCursor += e.length;
		tick().then(() => {
			composerInput?.focus();
			composerInput?.setSelectionRange(emojiCursor, emojiCursor);
		});
	}

EDIT 4 — right after the sticker Modal block (lines 704-711, `{#if stickerOpen}` ... `{/if}`) insert:
	{#if emojiOpen}
		<Modal open onclose={() => (emojiOpen = false)} title="emoji">
			<EmojiPicker
				onselect={insertEmoji}
				onclose={() => (emojiOpen = false)}
			/>
		</Modal>
	{/if}

EDIT 5 — in the composer form, right after the sticker button (lines 764-772, ends with `</button>`) and before the message input (line 773), insert:
			<button
				type="button"
				class="btn shrink-0 px-3 py-3"
				aria-label="emoji"
				title="insert an emoji"
				onclick={openEmoji}
			>
				<Smile size={16} />
			</button>

EDIT 6 — the message input (lines 773-782, `<input class="min-w-0 flex-1 text-[15px]" bind:value={text} placeholder="say something to the room…" autocomplete="off" onpaste=... />`): add `bind:this={composerInput}` as the first attribute.

WHY: EmojiPicker is already imported (line 13); Modal is already imported (line 12); Smile (lucide outline) visually distinguishes the emoji button from the sticker button (🙂 text). Cursor-aware splice + focus restore is the standard chat-app behaviour. Insert-at-cursor is captured on open (selectionStart) because the modal steals focus.

TESTS: the rooms page has no page-level vitest harness (only component tests exist), so the gate for this step is: pnpm check (catches the Smile import, $state refs, tick usage) AND pnpm test (full suite stays green). Behavioral proof is the final browser step.

PHASES: 1) no new unit tests possible (page has no harness) — the failing check is the phase-2 witness: run `pnpm check` BEFORE editing and see it passes today; 2) make the 6 edits; 3) run `pnpm check` and `pnpm test` — both green; 4) done. (Browser-verified in the final step.)

